piotroski":7,"_gp_piotroski":true,"_score_piotroski":77.8,"_gate_spread":null,"_gp_spread":null,"_score_spread":null,"_gate_roic_consistency":null,"_gp_roic_consistency":null,"_score_roic_consistency":null,"_gate_incr_roic":null,"_gp_incr_roic":null,"_score_incr_roic":null,"_gate_margin_advantage":null,"_gp_margin_advantage":null,"_score_margin_advantage":null,"_gate_pool_share":0.027810307519950506,"_gp_pool_share":true,"_score_pool_share":51.1,"_gate_rev_durability":0.0449809471266327,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":47.5,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":null,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":null,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":null,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.03012437693971598,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":44.6,"_gate_share_shrink":-0.01641266390103513,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":70.5,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.007700717458148275,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":87.2,"_gate_insider_own":0.01916,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":12.8,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Central Pacific Financial Corp. operates as the bank holding company for Central Pacific Bank that provides a range of commercial banking products and services to businesses, professionals, and individuals in the United States. The company offers various deposit products and services, including checking, savings and time deposits, cash management and digital banking, trust, and retail brokerage services, as well as money market accounts and certificates of deposit. It also provides various lending activities, such as commercial, industrial, commercial real estate, and residential mortgage, home equity, and consumer loans; and other products and services comprising debit cards, internet and mobile banking, full-service ATMs, safe deposit boxes, international banking services, night depository facilities, foreign exchange, and wire transfers. In addition, the company offers wealth management products and services that include non-deposit investment products, annuities, insurance, investment management, asset custody and general consultation, financial advisory, and estate planning services. Central Pacific Financial Corp. was founded in 1954 and is headquartered in Honolulu, Hawaii.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Arnold D. Martines | Chairman, President & CEO | Age 60 | Compensation: $2.0M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 722 people. Revenue per employee of $405K ranks in the below the sector median among Financial Services peers. Each employee generates $128K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $3K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 5\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (3/10).","financial_summary":["Central Pacific Financial Corp  is a small-cap financial services business with a $974M market cap on $293M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +4% over the past three years and +4% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 11% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business barely earns its keep economically.","The business throws off $92M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 32 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.26\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.7\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and thin 1.4\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 3.0% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.2) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 51% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Piotroski score 7/9 \u2014 financials improving across profitability, leverage and efficiency","13 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Financial quality scores above most Financial Services peers"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Are You Looking for a Top Momentum Pick? Why Central Pacific Financial (CPF) is a Great Choice","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3022064/are-you-looking-for-a-top-momentum-pick-why-central-pacific-financial-cpf-is-a-great-choice?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Cyseop_te